# Move the Alnasl hall box to the next release train (v7 -> v8), without a screen.
#
# Inside its train a box updates by itself at night (7.0 -> 7.1 -> 7.2). A new train
# never installs by itself: it is asked for, in the menu (Settings > System updates >
# "Upgrade to v8"), on Arkab's page, or with this file.
#
# To use it: make a file called "alnasl-upgrade.txt" in this folder whose FIRST line is
# the train, for example v8 (nothing else on that line), and boot the Pi with a network.
# This example does not count as it is: its first line is this comment.
#
# At boot the box deletes the file first (so it cannot happen twice), waits for the
# network, downloads the newest v8 image, checks its signature, writes it next to the
# running system and restarts into it. If v8 does not start properly three times, the
# box goes back to the version it had by itself. Not during a round: then nothing
# happens and the result (Settings > System updates, or the diagnostics) says so.
